{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions","id":970832,"title":"[2E] Healing Health related Conditions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-16T12:31:29-07:00","id":970832,"title":"[2E] Healing Health related Conditions","content":"In one of my games, I have PC that lost sight in previous story. Player wants to restore it back. He has Blind as Condition on char sheet.<br /> <br /> <b>\u200bHow much Life do need other mage to resolve it permanently?</b> Could other Arcana help with that?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:37:42-07:00","id":970836,"title":"","content":"Life Patterning but it t won't be Lasting, just Indefinite.<br /> <br /> Forces Unveiling would also work, or possibly Space Unveiling.<br /> <br /> Time Unveiling might be fun if you don't mind being a few seconds out of sync in the past or future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:43:41-07:00","id":970838,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions#post970832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In one of my games, I have PC that lost sight in previous story. Player wants to restore it back. He has Blind as Condition on char sheet.<br /> <b>\u200bHow much Life do need other mage to resolve it permanently?</b> Could other Arcana help with that?</div> </div> </div> </div>You're not going to make it Lasting with Life. The spell that regenerates organs and addresses conditions like this only lasts for as long as the duration of the spell, so Indefinite is your best bet.<br /> Better off creating (or finding) and binding a spirit of healing and making it do the dirty work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:44:13-07:00","id":970839,"title":"","content":"Need more details. Was this character born blind, or did they lose their sight due to injury? If the latter, was the damage irreversible (was it caused by aggravated damage), or can it be healed (was it caused by lethal or bashing damage)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:44:22-07:00","id":970840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=970836#post970836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life Patterning but it t won't be Lasting, just Indefinite.</div> </div> </div> </div>And there is no way to make it into Lasting?<br /> <br /> If I remember rules on Indefinite it's still eats spell slot on character and can comes with unknown spells effects if original caster will die?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=970836#post970836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forces Unveiling would also work, or possibly Space Unveiling.</div> </div> </div> </div>He use self cast Space Unveiling ( called simply 'Echolocation' by us ), but it's always slot eater - and not possible to read things ( as Space is only working like Daredevil senses ), so as Mysterium mage it's a big hindrance to have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=970836#post970836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time Unveiling might be fun if you don't mind being a few seconds out of sync in the past or future.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting, even if it's next spell slot eater.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:47:54-07:00","id":970845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=970839#post970839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was this character born blind, or did they lose their sight due to injury?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was injury. He get one on operation table, when his 'doctor' got Dramatic Failure on one roll of saving his life with Medicine Skill. Character is now second week without sight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=970839#post970839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the latter, was the damage irreversible (was it caused by aggravated damage), or can it be healed (was it caused by lethal or bashing damage)?</div> </div> </div> </div>It was Condition applied from life saving operation - going from Aggravated to Lethal damage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:51:21-07:00","id":970851,"title":"","content":"If you're worried about spell slots, Safely Relinquishing spells is a thing.<br /> <br /> Spirit still seems like your best bet, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:53:40-07:00","id":970852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=970845#post970845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was injury. He get one on operation table, when his 'doctor' got Dramatic Failure on one roll of saving his life with Medicine Skill. Character is now second week without sight.<br /> <br /> It was Condition applied from life saving operation - going from Aggravated to Lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if it's permanent (i.e., not tied to the damage in his leftmost health box), you can't make it Lasting with Life. You can cast it with Indefinite Duration and basically cross that spell control slot off the sheet because it'll always be going to maintaining the spell, or you can Relinquish the spell for a Willpower dot (though it will still be at risk of being Dispelled, either way).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T12:55:33-07:00","id":970853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=970840#post970840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And there is no way to make it into Lasting?<br /> <br /> If I remember rules on Indefinite it's still eats spell slot on character and can comes with unknown spells effects if original caster will die?<br /> <br /> He use self cast Space Unveiling ( called simply 'Echolocation' by us ), but it's always slot eater - and not possible to read things ( as Space is only working like Daredevil senses ), so as Mysterium mage it's a big hindrance to have.<br /> <br /> Interesting, even if it's next spell slot eater.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it can't be made Lasting, if spell slots are a worry then just safely Relinquish it. No unknown spell effects then. All the solutions I listed will be a spell slot eater.<br /> <br /> @Inodiv has a good suggestion though it can be broader than Spirit, summon an entity with healing powers and command it or make a bargain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:37:53-07:00","id":970884,"title":"","content":"I don't have my Mage PDF handy at work, but as someone above observed, if the blindness is still essentially an &quot;injury&quot; not received from aggravated damaged, and the character's eyes are still basically intact, couldn't the damage be just healed (i.e., Lasting) like normal lethal (or aggravated) damage?<br /> <br /> If that's not possible under the rules, I second the bartering with spirits suggestion, or similar alternatives such as seeking help after summoning an appropriate supernal entity or obtaining an artifact or imbued object that compensates for or restores vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-16-2016, 05:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T13:46:00-07:00","id":970891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=970884#post970884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have my Mage PDF handy at work, but as someone above observed, if the blindness is still essentially an &amp;quot;injury&amp;quot; not received from aggravated damaged, and the character's eyes are still basically intact, couldn't the damage be just healed (i.e., Lasting) like normal lethal (or aggravated) damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, if it was from a non-aggravated injury you could just heal the damage (which can be made Lasting) to heal the Tilt, as per the rules for the Tilt itself. If the injury was from aggravated damage, or the Tilt was caused by other means than damage (such as being born blind, or as was the case here, the result of a dramatically failed roll), there's no associated damage to heal, and Life doesn't have any spells that cure Tilts and can be made Lasting. I guess you might be able to create one that does with creative casting, but that's subject to ST discretion.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=970884#post970884\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If that's not possible under the rules, I second the bartering with spirits suggestion, or similar alternatives such as seeking help after summoning an appropriate supernal entity or obtaining an artifact or imbued object the compensates or restores vision.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's probably the safest approach, and part of why Spirit is an amazing Arcanum. Can't do something with your own magic? Get a spirit to do it for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T14:09:58-07:00","id":970906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=970891#post970891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That's probably the safest approach, and part of why Spirit is an amazing Arcanum. Can't do something with your own magic? Get a spirit to do it for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bargaining with inhuman entities out of desperation (or trying to compel them and most assuredly making enemies for life), what could possibly go wrong... ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> At that rate, you could also seek out one of those crazy archmasters. I hear they're always willing to lend a hand (or eye)...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T14:12:44-07:00","id":970910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=970906#post970906\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bargaining with inhuman entities out of desperation (or trying to compel them and most assuredly making enemies for life), what could possibly go wrong... ? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> At that rate, you could also seek out one of those crazy archmasters. I hear they're always willing to lend a hand (or eye)...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, maybe &quot;safe&quot; isn't the best word...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T14:35:39-07:00","id":970921,"title":"","content":"Either way the &quot;solution&quot; will be permanent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T15:15:39-07:00","id":970940,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=970839#post970839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Need more details. Was this character born blind, or did they lose their sight due to injury? If the latter, was the damage irreversible (was it caused by aggravated damage), or can it be healed (was it caused by lethal or bashing damage)?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster </strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was Condition applied from life saving operation - going from Aggravated to Lethal damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could find a Horror with effects like <a href=\"http://www.scp-wiki.net/scp-679\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 09-16-2016, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-16T21:57:29-07:00","id":971150,"title":"","content":"Side ( but related ) topic: The same character had <i>Megalomaniacal</i> Condition from failed Wisdom roll. He asked Mind Adept and she helped him with one simple spell. Was it by the book ruling? <b>Can Mind Adept resolve Permanent Mind-related Conditions ( even if they come from Wisdom roll failure )?</b><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=970891#post970891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, if it was from a non-aggravated injury you could just heal the damage (which can be made Lasting) to heal the Tilt, as per the rules for the Tilt itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>But non-aggravated injury would just make Tilt last to the end of combat, not permanent 'and you are blind from then on', yes? I try to understand a difference in rules interpretation, as from what I know, Adept's magic should be able to undone Condition and Tilts with spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=970891#post970891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the injury was from aggravated damage, or the Tilt was caused by other means than damage (such as being born blind, or as was the case here, the result of a dramatically failed roll), there's no associated damage to heal, and Life doesn't have any spells that cure Tilts and can be made Lasting. I guess you might be able to create one that does with creative casting, but that's subject to ST discretion.</div> </div> </div> </div>Will wait for answer on Mind-related Conditions here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=970891#post970891\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's probably the safest approach, and part of why Spirit is an amazing Arcanum. Can't do something with your own magic? Get a spirit to do it for you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Very good and interesting idea! If Life magic will not resolve problem, we will probably use Spirit summoning then. Oh, <i>nothing</i> bad can go wrong with that... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T01:16:33-07:00","id":971200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=971150#post971150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Very good and interesting idea! If Life magic will not resolve problem, we will probably use Spirit summoning then. Oh, <i>nothing</i> bad can go wrong with that... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I've been suggesting it since the third post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> For Mind magic, it doesn't seem to have the same restrictions that Life apparently does re: Persistent Conditions, from what I can see. Clear Thoughts should work on any mental condition, persistent or otherwise.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T02:08:54-07:00","id":971213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=971150#post971150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But non-aggravated injury would just make Tilt last to the end of combat, not permanent 'and you are blind from then on', yes? I try to understand a difference in rules interpretation, as from what I know, Adept's magic should be able to undone Condition and Tilts with spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Something like a spitting cobra or mace sprayed in the character's eyes? A flashbang grenade's effects? Those things should be pretty easily curable by Life magic, yes. A simple Life spell can help flush the toxin, but to heal the Condition would require further magic. I wrote a small section in Hurt Locker to address supernatural healing and durability with Conditions/Tilts and Extreme Environments. If you suffer Blinded from something besides an injury, curing it is fairly simple. Basically, you heal the Tilt in place of a point of lethal damage (bashing for Deafened), though for mages, the answer's already there under Knit (Life 3, p. 150). With a Reach, you can heal physical Personal Tilts, such as Arm Wrack. This doesn't extend to Conditions that temporarily act as Tilts, such as if your character is permanently suffering the Blind Condition, which acts as the Blinded Tilt in combat. But if you're blinded by pepper spray, you can &quot;spend&quot; a single point of lethal damage you would have otherwise healed through some means to recover from it, or simply use Knit with the proper Reach.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T05:53:11-07:00","id":971279,"title":"","content":"Look at Knit and Regeneration.<br /> <br /> Creative Thaumaturgy says that removing a condition is always at least a Ruling (**) spell and otherwise follows the same rules as creating them.<br /> <br /> That means removing a Persistent Condition is Patterning or Unraveling, as makes sense to the Arcana and Condition present. For physical Persistent Conditions, this is probably in the purview of Regeneration, which requires Potency 2 to affect eyes and cannot be made Lasting. Why? Hell if I know. Other healing spells are Lasting. They are basically the one type of spell specifically called out as Lasting in the sidebar. Lasting rules are inconsistent and make no sense. But there you have it.<br /> <br /> Mind lets you cure mental Conditions with Clear Thoughts (***) instead of four dots, and with two reach it can make it Lasting. It cannot affect Conditions granted by Paradox, but it says nothing about either Wisdom or Persistent Conditions. This means it probably works on both. Psychic Reprogramming can also muck with Conditions, but there is no Lasting option. Neither option grants Beats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T06:35:26-07:00","id":971299,"title":"","content":"Double post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T06:35:26-07:00","id":971300,"title":"","content":"I'm more in camp of making <i>Regeneration</i> as Lasting healing of Persistent Condition,<i> if </i>other spells Life and Mind spells can cure Lasting damage and Conditions.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=971279#post971279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That means removing a Persistent Condition is Patterning or Unraveling, as makes sense to the Arcana and Condition present. For physical Persistent Conditions, this is probably in the purview of Regeneration, which requires Potency 2 to affect eyes and cannot be made Lasting. Why? Hell if I know. Other healing spells are Lasting. They are basically the one type of spell specifically called out as Lasting in the sidebar. Lasting rules are inconsistent and make no sense. But there you have it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Checked both <i>Mend</i> and <i>Knit</i> spells - nothing in the write up points directly as Lasting healing. Maybe I miss something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-17-2016, 09:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T08:04:22-07:00","id":971321,"title":"","content":"Regeneration explicitly isn't Lasting in the write-up.<br /> <br /> As for Healing spells being Lasting, look at the sidebar for Lasting on page 113.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T09:44:14-07:00","id":971362,"title":"","content":"Well, it's bizarre then. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Lasting sidebar literally mentions:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MtAw 2E, p. 113</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wounds healed with magic do not reopen when the spell\u2019s Duration ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Regeneration 'heals' your lost eyes or limbs, it should then left is at healed state. Especially, with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar109_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"109\" data-vbnamecard=\"109\">Claire Redfield</a> clarification from Hurt Locker. <b>What is real difference between healing eyes from Blind Tilt in combat time and healing them from Blind Condition that is outside of it? </b>It works on <i>literally </i>the same principles of magic, where mage is making instant cellular regeneration.<br /> <br /> Especially when Mind magic can cure any Permanent insanity-related Conditions. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <b>So you can get total mental health from Mastigos in one go, but need to return specially for your physical health to Thyrsus?</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T09:58:20-07:00","id":971367,"title":"","content":"If the Blind Condition represents a permanent blindness, such as having your eyes destroyed by acid or some kind of curse, then you'd have to more or less regenerate the eyes to cure it. That is by the rules an impermanent solution. Healing damage done to the eyes before it has a chance to become permanent is easier than regrowing them from zero functionality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:27:40-07:00","id":971385,"title":"","content":"In this particular example is more 'some nerves are hit hard in you skull', so lesser magic should work. Even then, it's really weird that <i>you can make yourself free of your childhoods greatest phobia in one go</i> with Mind magic but to recreate organs you need to recast spell every while.<br /> <br /> Like, you lost hand in accident three days ago and it's something greater problem on your own Pattern than insanity that was growing on you one and half decade now? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-17-2016, 01:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T10:36:20-07:00","id":971391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=971279#post971279\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lasting rules are inconsistent and make no sense. But there you have it.</div> </div> </div> </div>This pretty much sums up the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:17:00-07:00","id":971416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=971391#post971391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This pretty much sums up the thread.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I anticipate that we'll receive greater clarification on Lasting (among other issues) in the upcoming Mage FAQ. I both hope and fear that the Mage FAQ might rival the size of the corebook in light of the myriad of issues raised in the FAQ thread and continuing in so many other posts.<br /> <br /> Given the magic system's complexity and extreme versatility and open-endedness, a Mage FAQ is really required to avoid unnecessary disputes and disagreements far more than many other games, both WW and otherwise.<br /> <br /> I know Dave's very busy with Deviant, other paid WW writing assignments and real life, but I think he should prioritize the FAQ even above other highly desired promised bonus material such as the antagonist and legacies material.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":618,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","user":"branford","date":". 09-17-2016, 02:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T11:45:41-07:00","id":971428,"title":"","content":"Eh, it's damned annoying, but I'd rather keep being intrigued by new content than continually hashing over the old stuff when it can usually be handled by a sensible ruling via the ST.<br /> <br /> I mean, I do agree, better parameters for Lasting and Conjunctional, etc spell effects would be very well received, but in the end it's the story and materials for building more of them that matters most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T12:48:59-07:00","id":971469,"title":"","content":"The spells are part of the story and it would be good to know how to judge what can be Lasting and what not. It directly influences the story. The system is so much better than 1E but there are some inconsistencies in the book so you can't deduce whats a correct way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T13:02:11-07:00","id":971483,"title":"","content":"I'm not disagreeing with that, I'm just saying that I don't think the priority should be on revising old stuff when there's new stuff we can look forward to.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T13:16:58-07:00","id":971487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=971483#post971483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not disagreeing with that, I'm just saying that I don't think the priority should be on revising old stuff when there's new stuff we can look forward to.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it <i>is</i> priority, as I want to remind you all we do not have <u>final</u> version of new corebook still. Developers should look over of those things till is time before PoD version.<br /> <br /> <b>If Mind magic works one way, and Life magics works other - they should be made consistent before final version of corebook.</b><br /> <br /> I would rather wait one more month for fixing problem with <b>Mage</b> corebook than get <b>Signs of Sorcery</b> or <b>Deviant</b>. On broken rules game is much more headache to run and will get worse reviews on final release.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T13:21:01-07:00","id":971490,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=971487#post971487\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>If Mind magic works one way, and Life magics works other - they should be made consistent before final version of corebook.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Why? What if they're just different?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T14:02:47-07:00","id":971514,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=971490#post971490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why? What if they're just different?</div> </div> </div> </div>The same reason why Practices follow the same theme. Or why Arcana Attainments are spread like they are. In setting it's 'basic principles of magic'. Out of game it's simple game balance and rules consistency.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-18-2016, 12:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-17T15:28:18-07:00","id":971539,"title":"","content":"Because in a game with Creative Thaumaturgy that expects you to design your own spell effects, there needs to be solid and consistent guidelines or nobody has a clue what they're doing.<br /> <br /> If they work differently, the exception should probably be explained.<br /> <br /> Otherwise, you end up with players not knowing what to expect because there are inconsistent and contradictory standards and the Storytellers doing way more work than they should have to because there is no solid guideline in place.<br /> <br /> The Practices and Arcana Purviews go a long way towards this, as do the guidelines in the Creative Thaumaturgy section, but what qualifies as Lasting is all over the place and a source of problems in just about every community I've looked into. This thread is a prime example. I'm hoping there's a solid clarification upcoming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-26T23:14:35-07:00","id":976998,"title":"","content":"I'm wanting to hack rules so those 'Condition resolving' effects would be Lasting, like Life 4 <i>Regeneration</i> spell. How will this change spells? Like it will have written 'Duration: Lasting' on it? Or do it need Reach effect for that?<br /> <br /> On quick search, most spells have +2 Reach Lasting effect for 1 Mana. Irritating are that there are some spells that are just Lasting from start, like in Spirit Arcanum, without any Reach spend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 09-27-2016, 02:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T00:55:02-07:00","id":977053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=976998#post976998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm wanting to hack rules so those 'Condition resolving' effects would be Lasting, like Life 4 <i>Regeneration</i> spell. How will this change spells? Like it will have written 'Duration: Lasting' on it? Or do it need Reach effect for that?<br /> <br /> On quick search, most spells have +2 Reach Lasting effect for 1 Mana. Irritating are that there are some spells that are just Lasting from start, like in Spirit Arcanum, without any Reach spend. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If it makes sense for the spell to be lasting by default (most damage spells and most healing spells), there's no need for a Reach effect to 'make' it lasting. For something that's resolving conditions, I would follow the model set by Clear Thoughts, and change the language to reflect physical conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T02:11:28-07:00","id":977077,"title":"","content":"Lasting regeneration means less people having to depend on mages to keep their regrown arms and legs from falling off every month.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd just steal someone else's organs and use a 3 dot spell to graft them in like a back alley surgeon.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11641-yelesom","name":"Yelesom","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11641_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:29:49-07:00","id":977114,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yelesom</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=977077#post977077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lasting regeneration means less people having to depend on mages to keep their regrown arms and legs from falling off every month.<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd just steal someone else's organs and use a 3 dot spell to graft them in like a back alley surgeon.</div> </div> </div> </div>And here <b>yourself <i>omits one month recast </i></b>- so you see how this is silly leftover of beta phase. Especially as Mind 3 spell <i>Clear Thoughts</i> can do the same with Mental Conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T04:33:55-07:00","id":977116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/970832-2e-healing-health-related-conditions?p=977053#post977053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If it makes sense for the spell to be lasting by default (most damage spells and most healing spells), there's no need for a Reach effect to 'make' it lasting. For something that's resolving conditions, I would follow the model set by Clear Thoughts, and change the language to reflect physical conditions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I checked both 2E <b>Mage</b> corebook and it's errata - and Mind 3 <i>Clear Thoughts</i> <b>is</b> using +2 Reach for Lasting. It does not count Mana for it, still. For Life 4<i> Regeneration</i> I would use Mana price still, though, as it is more powerfull effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-27T11:14:41-07:00","id":977264,"title":"","content":"On page 128 of 2E <b>Mage</b> corebook is official rule on making spells Lasting:<br /> <br /> 'Making a spell Lasting always costs +2 Reach, but you should think carefully before allowing it \u2014 only spells without any way to revert them should have the option.'<br /> <br /> Myself, I just hack Life 4 <i>Regeneration </i>that it can use this option, only it costs Mana equal to needed Potency for regrowing organ. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}